      "summary": "Cardrona There is no skiing at Cardrona right now — the resort closed at 1pm today due to worsening wind, after a genuinely scrappy operational day. It opened this morning with lifts on wind hold, but conditions deteriorated through the day: Willows closed early, Soho was called at 11:40am, Captains and the basin followed at 11:54am, and the final word came at 12:10pm — carpets, the T-Bar, and Valley View closing at 1pm, with a Platter closure at 12:20pm and shuttle transport running from Valley View back to base for anyone caught up there. Currently -1°C with wind at 47 km/h, gusting to 89 km/h. On the snow side, there's real substance to build on: 15cm fell in the past 24 hours (17cm over 7 days), landing on a firm base with wind-affected texture and variable off-trail conditions, for a natural snow depth of 115cm at 1800m. All 10 lifts are now closed — Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express, Willow's Quad, and Wells Pipe Platter — along with every terrain park and named zone (Baby Bucks through Big Air, Gravity Cross, and all marked terrain from Learners Slopes to the Summit). (Issued: 12:10 pm, 5 Sep) Roads are chain-free today (chains must still be carried), though an active road hazard advisory is in effect. Today's Masters Ski Racing event in the main basin was cancelled at 9:10am given conditions; the Pipeline mini pipe comp in the People's Pipe was still slated to go ahead. With neighbouring Queenstown mountains also shut today, Cardrona flagged busier-than-usual car parking and asked for patience with road crews. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 8 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
